What this project distributes, and under what terms.

The eight runtime dependencies are all MIT: `@lydell/node-pty`,
`@radix-ui/react-select`, `@xterm/xterm`, `@xterm/addon-fit`, `electron-updater`,
`react`, `react-dom`, and `zustand`. The desktop application also carries
Electron, which brings Chromium and Node.js; their licence texts ship beside the
executable as `LICENSE.electron.txt` and `LICENSES.chromium.html`.

Build-time tooling is not redistributed and is therefore not covered by that
sentence. It is a larger tree under more varied terms — permissive for the most
part, with some file-level copyleft (MPL-2.0) and other licences among the
transitive development dependencies.

