A note kept for the record, because a guard outlived what it guarded.

This project once had one dependency that was not open source:
`@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`, published under Anthropic's own terms
("© Anthropic PBC. All rights reserved"). It was a build-time dependency of an
optional runtime adapter, and both the adapter and the dependency have since
been removed.

`scripts/package.mjs` still refuses to package any bundle containing that
dependency's markers, and the check stays deliberately. It never fired: the
adapter was not registered in any headless entry point, so proprietary code
reached no distributed bundle by accident rather than by construction. Packaging
is where redistribution would actually happen — not at build, not at install —
so that is where the refusal belongs, ready for the next proprietary SDK that
arrives as a convenience inside one adapter.
